{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels especially relevant because my interest in Old Sock carries over to its relaxed, Clapton-connected roots sound.",
    "Gary Clark Jr. Live and Different Shades Of Blue connect with the blues-guitar interest reflected in People, Hell & Angels; Gary Clark Jr. Live is the one I would explore first."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "New and Yesterday And Today do not fit what I want today: a familiar connection to rock is less compelling than blues guitar and roots music.",
    "Duets feels less appealing than a focused blues album, while CSNY 1974 interests me but feels like too large a listening commitment for this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad interest in classic rock as enough reason for me to choose another release.",
    "They seem to assume that familiar artists, compilations, and catalogue revisits appeal equally to me, even though I would rather explore a release that fits my current mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Old Sock and relaxed, blues-rooted listening matters more to me today than a general rock connection.",
    "An album can fit my taste without making me want to act now; I would choose only the strongest matches, especially The Breeze and Gary Clark Jr. Live."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in blues and roots-oriented rock but spread too broadly into familiar rock releases that I would not choose today."
}"}
